## What I did

Fixed the saturated emerging-momentum signal in src/commands_risk_emerging.rs.

The bug: compute_momentum(c7, c30) = (c7/7)/(c30/30) collapses to the constant `30/7 ≈ 4.29 whenever a file's only changes fall inside the 7-day window (c7 == c30) — regardless of magnitude. So compute_momentum(1,1) == compute_momentum(2,2)`. Any such file ties at the top of the anticipatory ranking, and the emerging column can't discriminate among them. This matters for the dream's epistemic milestone: the "columns disagree" blind-spot signal is fed by reactive-vs-emerging disagreement, and if the emerging column is saturated, that disagreement could be a momentum artifact rather than real information.

The fix (approach b — the smaller, clearer one): Added `const MIN_MOMENTUM_SAMPLES: u32 = 3` with a doc comment explaining the saturation. Files with fewer than 3 total changes over the 30-day window are now excluded from the emerging list — an explicit third value (not eligible), not an accidental absorption at saturated-high momentum into the top bucket (Day-144 abstention-case discipline).

Tests first (red-green): I wrote three tests before the fix and watched them fail to compile (const didn't exist), then pass:
• `test_momentum_saturates_when_all_changes_recent — pins the degenerate behavior: compute_momentum(1,1) == compute_momentum(2,2) == 30/7`.
• `test_low_sample_files_are_damped_or_excluded` — a genuine burst (5-in-7d vs 8-in-30d) survives; a saturated 2-sample file is excluded, no tie.
• `test_min_momentum_samples_boundary_passes — the near-miss side (Day-122 lesson): a file with *exactly* MIN_MOMENTUM_SAMPLES` changes is admitted (guard is "below MIN").

Scope respected: touched only `commands_risk_emerging.rs + a one-line CLAUDE.md note. No existing test deleted. compute_momentum`'s pure behavior is unchanged (the guard lives in the detect path, so the compute_momentum(3,0)==3.0 new-hotspot case still holds).

